{"kind":"request","text":"Open a Question's detail when only its summary exceeds the card budget\n\nScope: the proposal in report 38543fe9 under bd2b5337, with evidence in ~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-04-question-summary-budget-investigation (SHA256SUMS 11e85369...). Today the adapter checks the 60 KiB serialized card before the session removes long-text summary acts. The summary still carries the hidden body, and its Open wording adds 51 bytes. A Question whose detail fits at 61,440 bytes therefore shows an incomplete summary with no Open, and the person cannot reach the detail.\n\nBuild the proposal: budget the complete detail from one context first. If the detail fits but exceeds the first-card text bounds, build a compact navigation summary with the same identity and attribution, without the hidden body or native actions. Keep both byte limits and the rule against truncated text next to an act.\n\nWitness: the unchanged source fails ready-summary on the boundary case; the repaired source opens to the exact whole text; one more body byte refuses. Keep the short-text and UTF-8 boundary cases. Run the Card workflow on the exact head.\n\nOrder: after dc800768 and the O4 live runs, ahead of 0466ff4e. It changes the card for every host, not only Goose. The Goose host-size result stays not reached.","body":{"conditions":"Reviewed head lands on main with the boundary witness and a Card workflow pass at the exact head.","target_head":"60b908277c9adcb08560d0df679e7da90fbb4352","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}